# HEXA60 — Commercial IP Acquisition Notice

Copyright (c) 2026 Ladislav Muller. All rights reserved.

## 1. What this notice covers

This repository is offered as a **Commercial IP Package**: a deterministic
binary-to-text encoding technology (specification + Python reference
implementation + header-only C++20 implementation + native nanobind
accelerator + test suite + measured audit logs).

## 2. Evaluation vs acquisition

- **Evaluation:** you may clone, build (`python build_native.py`), run the
  test suite (`pytest tests/`) and reproduce the audit logs in `benchmarks/`
  for internal evaluation purposes only.
- **Acquisition / commercial use:** any integration into proprietary or
  closed-source products, SaaS, hardware appliances, redistribution, or
  removal of this notice requires a **written Commercial / IP Assignment
  agreement** with the rights holder.

## 3. Dual-licensing background

Unless covered by a commercial agreement, the code remains under the
**GNU AGPLv3** terms stated in `LICENSE-v2.md` (copyleft applies, including
network use). A commercial agreement replaces AGPL obligations with
proprietary terms, or assigns the IP outright — subject to negotiation.

